  },
  {
    "id": "alorair-sentinel-hd35p-pump",
    "name": "AlorAir Sentinel HD35P Dehumidifier with Pump",
    "category": "35 PPD at AHAM, Built-In Pump, Rated Down to 33.8°F",
    "badge": "Best for Crawl Spaces",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Spec sheet lists an operating range of 33.8°F to 110°F with auto defrost",
      "Built-in condensate pump and memory starting after a power cut",
      "Metal cabinet only 11.4 inches tall, built for continuous unattended running",
      "Draws just 2.9 amps, per AlorAir's specification sheet"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Does not appear on the current ENERGY STAR Version 6.0 certified list",
      "35 pints at 80°F AHAM conditions is less than a 50-pint portable in a warm basement"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick for an encapsulated crawl space or a cold, unfinished basement where mold grows on joists and a plastic portable would ice up and quit.",
    "description": "Crawl spaces are where a lot of household mold starts, on floor joists and subfloor sheathing that sit above damp soil, and they are a poor home for a plastic portable. The HD35P is built for that job. AlorAir's specification sheet lists 35 pints per day at AHAM conditions (80°F, 60% relative humidity) and 70 at saturation, for spaces up to about 1,000 square feet, with an operating range of 33.8°F to 110°F and an automatic defrost system. That cold-weather floor is the reason to buy it: most portables are rated only to about 41°F and lose much of their output well before that. A built-in condensate pump removes the water, memory starting brings it back after a power cut, and the low-profile metal cabinet measures 15.35 by 11.2 by 11.4 inches and weighs 39.7 pounds. It draws 2.9 amps, moves 115 CFM and is listed at 55 dBA. AlorAir currently advertises a six-year limited warranty on its dehumidifiers, with the first two years of full coverage. One honest note: the 2023 spec sheet mentions ENERGY STAR, but the model is not on the current Version 6.0 list. Prices on Amazon usually run about $400 to $550."
  },
  {
    "id": "hisense-ahd5024k1w",
    "name": "Hisense AHD5024K1W 50-Pint Dehumidifier",
    "category": "50 Pints/Day, Rated to 38°F, 2-Year Warranty",
