    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "70 pints per day at 80°F/60% from a 12 by 12 by 21 inch cabinet",
      "Six-year manufacturer warranty, the longest in this guide",
      "Contractor brand built for year-round crawl space and basement duty",
      "About 580 watts and 5.1 amps on a standard 120-volt circuit"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Listed minimum operating temperature is 49°F",
      "No built-in pump, and it costs several times a portable"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "For a sealed crawl space or mechanical room in a mild climate where you want to install a dehumidifier once and forget it for years.",
    "description": "Santa Fe is the Therma-Stor brand that waterproofing and crawl space contractors have installed for decades, and the Compact70 is the model to buy if you want a mold-prevention unit that is designed to run for years rather than seasons. Santa Fe rates it at 70 pints per day at 80°F and 60% relative humidity, from a cabinet only 12 inches wide, 12 inches tall and 21 inches deep, so it slides through a small crawl space hatch. It moves about 150 CFM, draws roughly 580 watts and 5.1 amps, and Santa Fe sizes it for about 1,800 to 2,600 square feet of sealed crawl space. The six-year warranty is the longest of any pick here, and it reflects the fact that a crawl space unit may run several thousand hours a year. Two limits matter. Santa Fe lists a 49°F minimum operating temperature, which is fine in the South and in heated or partly conditioned spaces but not in a crawl space that sits in the low 40s all winter, where the AlorAir is the better tool. And there is no pump, so plan a gravity drain or a separate condensate pump. Expect roughly $1,400 to $1,650 on Amazon."
