            For most mold-prone basements without a floor drain, the Frigidaire FHDP5033Y1 is the dehumidifier to buy: a built-in pump with a gravity backup, auto restart after outages and an app that shows the humidity from anywhere. If the water has a long way to climb, the Midea Cube 50 with pump has the best published lift; for a crawl space or a basement that runs cold, the AlorAir Sentinel HD35P keeps working down to 33.8°F.
          </p>
